 paper's own wording.","citation_ids":["cite.step.construction_cover_not_weighted"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"step.construction_cover_not_weighted","kind":"claim","label":"A divisor cover with no finite-prime weighted condition","locator":"Proof of Proposition 5.1, pp. 11–12","source_id":"paper.short.pdf","statement":"With odd primes $q_j\\ge4^j$, disjoint prime sets $P_j$ and $V=\\bigcup_{j\\ge1}F_j$, $F_j=\\{q_jd:d\\mid M_j\\}$: $\\sum_{a\\in V}1/a$ diverges, $V\\notin\\mathcal W_b$ for every integer $b\\ge2$, and the choice $z_j=(j+S_j)^{-1}$, $\\alpha_j=\\log_2(1+z_j)$, $c_{j,q_jd}=z_j^{\\omega(d)}$ makes the cover cost summable, so $V\\in\\mathcal C$.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/step.construction_cover_not_weighted","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/short.res-weighted-cover-incomparability","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22short.res-weighted-cover-incomparability%22%2C%22step.construction_cover_not_weighted%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22short.res-weighted-cover-incomparability%22%2C%22step.construction_cover_not_weighted%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/step.construction_cover_not_weighted"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/step.construction_cover_not_weighted","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22step.construction_cover_not_weighted%22%2C%22step.cover_condition%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513